{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "reasoning", "text": "Looking at the baseline results,the current result is worse than the baseline, and my understanding of the scoring formula is incorrect. I've adjusted my focus to reducing the raw time directly as required.\n\nSeveral optimization paths have been sorted out, and the core optimization approach of deriving batch costs from dual potentials to eliminate redundant Sinkhorn solves has been confirmed. This simpler optimization will be implemented first, followed by checks for faster label cost computation methods. This optimization cuts per-pair work in half, and I'll test it locally.\n"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "agent_message", "text": "Let me analyze the baseline. Raw metric: ~0.956s/case. The current method.py IS the canonical baseline. The biggest bottleneck is doing both a POT Sinkhorn AND a GeomLoss solve per batch pair.\n\nLet me implement a key optimization: compute batchcost from the GeomLoss dual potentials directly, eliminating the separate POT Sinkhorn solve per pair. Then we only need one GeomLoss solve per pair (which also gives F).\n\nLet me first do a quick local test to validate accuracy of this approach.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/test_geomloss_bc.py << 'PYEOF'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Quick test: can we compute batchcost from GeomLoss potentials?\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nimport ot\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\n\nnp.random.seed(42)\nN, M = 500, 400\nx = np.random.randn(N, 10).astype(np.float32)\nr = np.random.randn(M, 10).astype(np.float32)\ny = np.random.randint(0, 10, N)\nry = np.random.randint(0, 10, M)\n\n# Build W (simplified, just random)\nW = np.random.rand(20, 20).astype(np.float32)\nW = (W + W.T) / 2\nnp.fill_diagonal(W, 0)\n\ndef cost(z1, z2):\n    d = torch.cdist(z1[:, :, :-1], z2[:, :, :-1]).square() / 2\n    return d + torch.as_tensor(W)[z1[:, :, -1].long().unsqueeze(2),\n                                  z2[:, :, -1].long().unsqueeze(1)] / 2\n\npotential = SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=np.sqrt(.1), debias=False,\n                        potentials=True, cost=cost, backend='tensorized')\n\n# POT-based batchcost\nC = cdist(x, r, 'sqeuclidean') / 2 + W[y[:, None], ry[None, :] + 10] / 2\nP = ot.sinkhorn(ot.unif(N), ot.unif(M), C / max(float(C.max()), 1e-12), .1)\npot_bc = float(np.sum(P * C)) / (N + M)\nprint(f\\\"POT batchcost: {pot_bc:.10f}\\\")\n\n# GeomLoss potentials\nz1 = torch.tensor(np.column_stack([x, y]), dtype=torch.float32)[None]\nz2 = torch.tensor(np.column_stack([r, ry + 10]), dtype=torch.float32)[None]\nwith torch.inference_mode():\n    f, g = potential(z1, z2)\nf_np = f.numpy().ravel().astype(float)\ng_np = g.numpy().ravel().astype(float)\n\n# Entropic cost = sum(a*f) + sum(b*g) = mean(f) + mean(g) (uniform weights)\nentropic_cost = f_np.mean() + g_np.mean()\nprint(f\\\"GeomLoss entropic cost: {entropic_cost:.10f}\\\")\n\n# Now try: sum(P*C) = sum(a*f) + sum(b*g) - reg*KL(P||a*b\"'^T)\n# For uniform weights: sum(a*f)+sum(b*g) = mean(f)+mean(g)\n# We need the primal cost sum(P*C), not entropic cost\n# Let'\"'s reconstruct P from potentials: P[i,j] = a[i]*b[j] * exp((f[i]+g[j] - C[i,j])/reg)\n# This works because: f[i] = reg * log(u[i]), where u from log-domain Sinkhorn\n# Actually GeomLoss uses different potential conventions...\n\n# Let's compute loss value directly\nloss_fn = SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=np.sqrt(.1), debias=False, backend='tensorized')\nwith torch.inference_mode():\n    loss_val = loss_fn(z1, z2)\nprint(f\\\"GeomLoss loss value: {float(loss_val):.10f}\\\")\n\n# The SamplesLoss('sinkhorn', p=2, blur=sigma, debias=False) computes \n# S_{p,blur}(alpha, beta) = OT_p\"'^p + regularization\n# Actually no - for sinkhorn loss, it returns the entropic OT cost\n# For blur=sigma, p=2: reg = sigma''^2 = 0.1\n\n# Let'\"'s check: sum(P*C) from POT vs GeomLoss loss\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nPOT primal (P*C)/(n+m): {pot_bc:.10f}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"GeomLoss loss: {float(loss_val):.10f}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"Ratio: {float(loss_val) / pot_bc:.6f}\\\")\n\n# Try with proper scaling\nC_max = float(C.max())\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nC_max = {C_max}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"POT reg = {0.1} (scaled by C_max)\\\")\nprint(f\\\"GeomLoss blur\"'^2 = {0.1} (not scaled)\")\nPYEOF\npython /tmp/test_geomloss_bc.py'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
